course: dictionary
lesson: 10725
title: Upbringing and how we are raised
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Your upbringing is the way your parents or carers raised you as a child: how they cared for you, taught you and what they believed was right. «Some parents are cold or distant because of their own stress or upbringing; it is not the child's fault.» Here, upbringing is the past that shaped a parent.
explain: Upbringing can also mean the place and the conditions you grew up in, such as a farm upbringing or a city upbringing. Look at the words just before it for clues. Strict, happy and religious are all describing an upbringing.
explain: «Some families run on very strict routines, often from a parent's job or upbringing; there is often a lot of love inside it.» So a strict routine can come from how someone was brought up, and strict does not mean unloving.
fact: Upbringing is a noun, usually singular: an upbringing.
fact: «A strict upbringing» means being raised with firm rules.
fact: «A happy upbringing» means a childhood full of care and good times.
fact: «Because of his upbringing» means the way he was raised helps explain why he thinks or acts as he does.
fact: Upbringing focuses on how you were cared for and taught, not just on how old you were.
exercise: In «Some parents are cold or distant because of their own stress or upbringing», what does upbringing mean? | *The way a parent was raised as a child | A type of school uniform | A parent's job at work | A holiday they took last year
exercise: Which phrase means raised with firm rules? | A quiet morning | A happy upbringing | *A strict upbringing | A farm holiday
exercise: Ella says, «Her upbringing was on a farm.» What does this tell us? | Where she likes to buy her shoes | *The place and conditions she grew up in | What she wants for her birthday | How tall she is
test: Sam always says thank you because of his upbringing. What does this tell us? | *His parents taught him good manners | He lives on a boat | He does not like food | He is always late for school
test: Which sentence uses upbringing correctly? | *Her religious upbringing shaped the way she thinks about kindness | We went to upbringing on Monday | Upbringing is a pet dog | Her upbringing is a red bus
exam: In a sentence about «a strict upbringing», which meaning of upbringing fits best? | A kind of cake | Holidays spent at the seaside | *The way a child was raised, with firm rules | The name of a school
